#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:5
#: 7debac87865545e3a6d03e0d8fc1591e
msgid "Hardware Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:7
#: 922af996925c46b29a4fa6fe859f6072
msgid "This page lists the hardware required for an autonomous Balance Bot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:10
#: 250b47ce3f644501b7da2703f6c7cece
msgid "Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:12
#: e4ee9fa99761493e824d7e9b7eca41be
msgid "Any readily available or custom made frame suitable for Balance Bots can be used. Ensure that there is sufficient space to hold all the components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:14
#: 3d1bdf72b2c745739151116fd89f8ab6
msgid "For a suitable starter example, check out :ref:`Yahboom Balance Bot<reference-frames-yahboom-balancebot>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:17
#: fd2a5cd63423430f80a552514b13fb9a
msgid "Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:19
#: 2824cfdde2e24cf392a585e8eda68f20
msgid "The autopilot needs at least two PWM outputs for controlling the two motors and four :ref:`GPIO pins<common-gpios>` to connect to two :ref:`wheel encoders <wheel-encoder>`.  Some autopilots without an IOMCU will not have enough GPIOs to support wheel encoders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:22
#: 605a0a0618494f329e2e7a432b2130de
msgid "Motors and Wheel Encoders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:24
#: 8ba4564617104e72a50c9575ed45bfff
msgid "The recommended solution is to use brushed motors with built-in quadrature :ref:`wheel encoders <wheel-encoder>` but other motors may be used if external encoders are attached to the motor shafts.  Note that only quadrature encoders with two output pins are supported.  :ref:`Wheel encoders <wheel-encoder>` allow faster and more precise control of each wheel which greatly improves the vehicle's balance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:26
#: 855cd209b5ba4a69b3d91ba94d42a3dd
msgid "Stepper Motors and motors that use UART/I2C interface are not currently supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:28
#: 06ee3a5e25fc4e45a9471c59f5a6bb5c
msgid "Gear backlash is a problem with many geared dc motors and this can negatively affect stability. It is recommended to use motors that are specified to be zero-backlash or have very little backlash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:31
#: 630d6ef7e87c4c6c9d1cc4ce57110ce7
msgid "ESCs/Motor Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:33
#: e876a26169b544d5803f5569453ecb2f
msgid "A list of verified ESCs/motor drivers can be fouind on the :ref:`brushed motors<common-brushed-motors>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:36
#: d89f04d0a22045b0a5551a3e97c002bb
msgid "GPS + Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:38
#: d34d6bccbfac4fe09c65ac649d73f101
msgid "A GPS+Compass module is recommended if the balance bot will be used outdoors in autonomous modes (e.g. Auto, Guided, RTL).  A compass is required so the vehicle can estimate its heading.  For more details on supported GPS hardware, refer to the :ref:`GPS/Compass page<common-positioning-landing-page>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:41
#: 707343baedb14f63b35fea682145e0e8
msgid "Telemetry Radio(optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-hardware.rst:43
#: b480f17d593d4e4d9c492997809458e9
msgid "Telemetry radios are very useful for tuning and debugging. For more information on supported hardware options refer :ref:`telemetry<common-telemetry-landingpage>` page."
msgstr ""
